	<Item Name="Accession" Type="String">GSE112734</Item>
	<Item Name="GDS" Type="String" />
	<Item Name="title" Type="String">A genome-wide screen identifies E2F6 as critical factor for TMZ chemoresistance in EGFRvIII expressing GBM (CRISPR library RNA-seq)</Item>
	<Item Name="summary" Type="String">We conducted a genome-wide screen by clustered regularly interspaced short palindromic repeats (CRISPR)-Cas9 library to identify genes which are particularly resistant to EGFRvIII GBM cells under the chemo-stress of TMZ. In vitro and in vivo validation of EGFRvIII-specific targets revealed several strong hits, including E2F6. Mechanistic studies demonstrated that E2F6 reveals its resistance to TMZ through NF-&#954;B and TMZ inducement.EGFRvIII GBM cells under the chemo-stress of TMZ.</Item>
